      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1qtb1hq'
    '|a||Those are transaction costs: the cost of striking and enforcing the deal itself. When they eat up the gain, no deal happens.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10gxgne'
    '|b||So the waste stays wherever the law left it. If the yard owns the bay, it dumps all the way to here.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:6i1avg'
    '|a||And this triangle is lost: harm to the fishers bigger than the yard''s savings, and nobody can afford to buy it away.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hjpt0y'
    '|b||Then who holds the right matters after all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2600
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ovgqwa'
    '|a||Which was Coase''s own point. He said the world without transaction costs was the world of economic theory, the one he hoped economists would leave.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:163er19'
    '|b||And a second crack: the endowment effect. Owners ask about twice what buyers offer, so whoever starts with the right tends to keep it, even when a deal costs nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:lgbl5r'
    '|a||Either way, the law''s first move shapes the outcome.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:3hbdqy'
    '|a||Transaction costs decide whether a deal can stand in for the law. So how often do real deals happen?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||In the lab, often. In Hoffman and Spitzer''s 1982 experiments, small groups reached the efficient deal in about nine decisions out of ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1i066yi'
    '|a||And outside the lab?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1g3m4xf'
    '|b||Bees. In 1973 Steven Cheung found apple growers and beekeepers in Washington State writing contracts for pollination, a spillover priced by private deals.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:18n5pb5'
    '|a||But neighbours who end up in court? Ward Farnsworth followed twenty nuisance cases, and in not one did the parties bargain after the judgment.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xhxgbq'
    '|b||The lawyers said bitterness was a big reason. And smog over a city, or the climate, involves millions. No table is that big.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1uosz8g'
    '|a||So: with no transaction costs the deal is efficient, which is logic, so consensus. That a few close parties often strike such deals is mostly agreed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:sm3jst'
    '|b||The arithmetic of the kitchen deal: open the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1v3nqqb'
    '|a||In the kitchen, the deal creates two hundred minus one hundred: a hundred dollars a week to share.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Any payment between one and two hundred leaves both better off. A hundred and fifty splits the gain evenly.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1f97fgd'
    '|a||And the deal happens only if that hundred is bigger than the cost of striking it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:k50k0z'
    '|b||Could a private deal fix it? Sort each case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1v5ak0t'
    '|a||Ann''s tree blocks Ben''s view. The law lets Ann keep it. The tree is worth $300 to Ann, the view $1,000 to Ben, and they talk easily. What happens?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10720
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Ben pays Ann somewhere between $300 and $1,000, and the tree comes down. The view is worth more.':
